  "description": "The closed shapes a proto_version 0.5 peer sends and receives. A telnet connect names term, cols and rows and carries no user and no auth: TSB types no vault secret into a stream. A telnet channel_opened reports the NAWS answer as resizable. The address check answers with error target_address_refused, naming the target id and never the address. A telnet connection's end is connection_lost cause single_session, its session_ids empty when the session's end has reached the core; at the bound, with a peer attached, it lists that session so the core reads its spool first.",
  "corpus": [
    "open_decisions §5",
    "Contract §15",
    "lang-arch §4.1",
    "session model §9 E2",
    "session model §11"
  ],
  "case": {
    "schema": "schemas/ipc-control.schema.json",
    "instances": [
      {
        "valid": true,
        "doc": {
          "cmd": "connect",
          "target_id": "fixture-target",
          "protocol": "telnet",
          "host": "192.0.2.10",
          "port": 23,
          "term": "xterm-256color",
          "cols": 120,
          "rows": 40,
          "timers": {
            "heartbeat_interval": 10000,
            "heartbeat_missed": 3,
            "keepalive_interval": 4000,
            "keepalive_count_max": 2,
            "keepalive_probe_interval": 1500,
            "connection_linger": 0,
            "orphan_timeout": 60000,
            "idle": 900000,
            "unattended": 1800000
          },
          "buffer_bytes": 65536,
          "input_frame_max": 4096
        },
        "note": "a telnet connect: term, cols and rows travel with it, no credential"
      },
      {
        "valid": true,
